HB0243 Denturist practice act.
Sponsored By: Representative(s) Winter
AN ACT relating to professions and occupations; amending licensing statutes for
dentists and dental hygienists to include denturists; authorizing a denturist
to be added to the board of dental examiners as specified; specifying that this
act does not apply to denturitry students performing denturitry as part of their
curriculum; specifying that denturists shall only perform dental laboratory
work at the direction of a dentist; requiring denturists and dental laboratory
technicians to complete work for a dentist pursuant to a written prescription
as specified; requiring dentists and denturists to engage the services of
persons outside their office with a written work authorization; specifying that
denturists in certain occupations are exempt from the act; specifying that
denturists may perform services for patients if trained to do so in an accredited
denturitry school and under the supervision of a dentist; amending requirements
relating to permissible supervised work by specified persons; requiring dental
hygienists to be graduates of a board approved program in order to practice;
amending definitions; providing definitions; amending other laws relating to
dentists and dental hygienists to include denturists as specified; providing an
appropriation; and providing for effective dates.
